      "writtenOn": "2020-05-27T03:10:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think WaitingForRestartState should be a substate of mTetheredState, otherwise you end up calling mTetheredState.exit() which tears down the downstream, then have Tethering stop tethering (which should also attempt to tear down the downstream); so this creates an unusual teardown path that\u0027s not well tested.\n\nYou could just do:\naddState(mTetheredState, mWaitingForRestartState)\nand you also don\u0027t need to handle CMD_TETHER_UNREQUESTED in WaitingForRestartState\n\nAlso that\u0027s assuming that this mechanism is not valid for local hotspot, so the handling of CMD_RESTART_TETHERING should be moved from BaseServingState to TetheredState",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 355,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 355,
        "endChar": 41
      },
